# Never convert line endings, on any machine and whatever core.autocrlf or GitHub Desktop is set to.
# Files check out byte for byte as stored, so source and deck fingerprints (project_manifest.json,
# deep_table.py, the add-on's source hashes) match everywhere. The engine's history stores many files
# with Windows line endings; converting them made a Windows clone show them all as changed.
* -text

# Shell scripts keep Unix line endings so bash in WSL can run them after a Windows checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The verified add-on wheel and engine program are kept byte for byte; their hashes are in project_manifest.json.
*.whl binary
rl/addon-0.7.2/deckgym binary
rl/engine-2026-09-25/deckgym binary
rl/engine-2026-09-25/legality_scan binary
rl/engine-2026-09-25/goldfish binary
